[18.2,"o","\u001b[2J\u001b[3;6H\u001b[1m$ noonsight report --log decisions.jsonl\u001b[0m\u001b[4;6H\u001b[90m… the experiment's log, this rule's lines:\u001b[0m\u001b[5;6Hsonnet-5-5/carry-through: 40 deliveries in 40 sessions, last 2026-11-20T21:16:45.275Z\u001b[6;6H   models: claude-sonnet-5-5 40\u001b[7;6H   scopes: build 40\u001b[8;6H   places: unattended 40\u001b[11;6H\u001b[1mThe measured example\u001b[0m\u001b[12;6HWith the rule carry-through delivered alone, Sonnet 5.5 did every part of a\u001b[13;6H13-ticket backlog in \u001b[1;33m32 of 40\u001b[0m runs, against \u001b[1;33m9 of 40\u001b[0m without any rule.\u001b[15;6H\u001b[90mMost of the difference is the one ticket shown. Evidence: R10 in docs/evidence.md.\u001b[0m\u001b[19;6H\u001b[1;33mWrite your own rules, per model.\u001b[0m noonsight delivers each rule to the model it is written for.\u001b[21;6H\u001b[1m$ npm install -g noonsight && noonsight install\u001b[0m\u001b[23;6Hgithub.com/bpsanti/noonsight"]
